cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SMRT in your research, please cite this software and the relevant publications listed in docs/References.md."
title: "SMRT: Gmsh-based preprocessing for two-dimensional Method of Characteristics neutron transport calculations"
abstract: >-
  SMRT is a Gmsh-based preprocessing tool that generates two-dimensional
  computational meshes and characteristic-line information for use with the
  ALPHA neutron lattice physics code. The current release supports square
  and hexagonal pin-cell geometries with structured and automatic mesh modes.
  SMRT does not include the neutron transport solver itself.
type: software
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: 2026-09-17
authors:
  - name: "CaoWei"
    affiliation: "ALPHA Group, Nuclear Reactor Physics, School of Physics, Zhejiang University"
keywords:
  - Gmsh
  - neutron transport
  - method of characteristics
  - lattice physics
  - characteristic-line tracking
  - mesh generation
license: MIT
